From: naelolaiz <1333555+naelolaiz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:19:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] main/htop: build without lm-sensors when bootstrapping

With BOOTSTRAP or APORTS_BOOTSTRAP set, leave out lm-sensors-dev, whose
package pulls in rrdtool, cairo and pango. htop's configure defaults
--enable-sensors to "check" and turns the feature off when
sensors/sensors.h is missing; htop loads libsensors with dlopen at run
time and only needs the header to build.

Without the variables the APKBUILD builds exactly what it built before.
Generic, not specific to riscv32.
---
 main/htop/APKBUILD | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/main/htop/APKBUILD b/main/htop/APKBUILD
index 6c1cf839e32..ef32a915c11 100644
--- a/main/htop/APKBUILD
+++ b/main/htop/APKBUILD
@@ -13,7 +13,11 @@ license="GPL-2.0-or-later"
 # Without this dependency, this screen doesn't emit an error
 # as busybox provides lsof but its output format is incompatible.
 depends="lsof"
-makedepends="ncurses-dev linux-headers lm-sensors-dev"
+makedepends="ncurses-dev linux-headers"
+if [ -z "$BOOTSTRAP" ] && [ -z "$APORTS_BOOTSTRAP" ]; then
+	# lm-sensors pulls in rrdtool, cairo and pango
+	makedepends="$makedepends lm-sensors-dev"
+fi
 subpackages="$pkgname-doc"
 source="https://github.com/htop-dev/htop/releases/download/$pkgver/htop-$pkgver.tar.xz"
 options="!check" # no upstream/available test-suite
-- 
